{"kind":"group","id":"b97bf956-8fb2-454d-8a0a-baa3ad3f7b26","type":"c552a431-af5b-46a9-a8a4-0fcbc27ef596","name":"Group","nick":"6 - Results: Von Mises stress on the vault, deformed 2000 times","desc":"A group of Grasshopper objects","box":[0,0,0,0],"colour":[40,42,45,49],"members":["f4b8b12f-8ffe-4d63-ab9b-b3b3137c8b30","46850b09-56fc-4bd7-bce7-b63ae98a8f74","29ef9f79-2d3e-41cf-96ab-cd596d8802b9"]},
{"kind":"panel","id":"b6b6473e-77a4-43bd-a4be-4dd65d499189","type":"59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c","name":"Panel","nick":"Vault of bricks","desc":"A panel for custom notes and text values","box":[300,60,900,200],"src":[],"text":"Vault of bricks - Mesh Loft and Mesh Series to Brick, from polylines to a solid.\n\nA concrete barrel vault 8 m across, 2.5 m high, 6 m long and 400 mm thick. The GhPython component draws it as polylines: Layers + 1 surfaces through its thickness, inside to outside, each a branch of polylines across the vault, one every brick along it, all with the same number of points - Mesh Loft needs that.\n\nMesh Loft lofts each branch into one mesh of quads. The meshes match face for face, so Mesh Series to Brick, taking them in order, makes a layer of bricks between each two: hexahedra, eight nodes each. SSP Brick turns them into elements of C30/37; both springings are held, every node along them.\n\nUnder its own weight the vault pushes outwards at its feet, and Model View colours it by Von Mises stress, drawn 2000 times its deformation: it works in compression, the stress highest along the feet, where its weight and its thrust meet the ground.\n\nTry: Rise 4 m, Layers of bricks 8, Thickness 0.25 m, and see how the stress moves.","colour":[255,255,250,90]}
